  "notes_for_annotators": "Inputs are numbered from 0. One encounter, from input 15, against a single giant crab, after a long build-up of checks. Vesna starts with lamp oil at quantity 0: the flask is in the inventory but empty, so input 3, a narration-only turn, should not find oil in it. Narration of oil sloshing in the flask there is a RESOURCE divergence. Oil goes 0, 2, 1 at inputs 6 and 22, and input 27 asks again, so one measure should be left. The spyglass is borrowed at input 8 and kept. Ilse starts at the top of the ladder, allied, goes down to friendly at input 9 and back up at input 24; the keeper goes up once from unfriendly to neutral. The single quest runs start, advance, advance, complete and ends at stage 3 of 3. Input 13 grants advantage because Vesna braces against the rail. Vesna is not a spellcaster and has no way to heal: input 26 invites a hit-point band phrase about her. Inputs 15 to 21 give more attacks than the fight usually needs; extra ones are rejected and do not advance the game."
